1800 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Connors: I thought they would be here already, but they're preparing to\leave just now... We might as well have lunch.":GOSUB 5100
1810 BM$="A waiter brought them to a table.":GOSUB 5100
1820 BM$="Connors: I bet he had some urgent business to take care of. They never\break their word once they give it, so...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1830 GOSUB 6315:BM$="Susanna: What do they do for a living? We only know he's someone\important. I kept thinking about it last night, I could barely sleep.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1840 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Connors: They raised me after I lost my parents... I owe them a debt I can\never repay. The least I can do is never break my promise to them. Sorry, I\can't say anything.":GOSUB 5100
1850 BM$="Connors: I couldn't believe this story either, that's why I sent that letter\to David. Honestly, I didn't think he'd actually show up.":GOSUB 5100
1860 BM$="Connors: I was surprised when David pretty much confirmed what that\person told me. He saw the Devil King in his dreams... What if everything else\is true as well? The thought alone gives me the shivers...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1870 GOSUB 6315:BM$="Susanna: Let me get this straight. While it's true the audience can get a bit\rowdy during David's concerts, no one actually gets hurt. It's the\opposite of what this person says.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1880 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Connors: I'm aware. I AM an entertainment reporter after all. I suppose it's\a good thing I never published that article in the end.":GOSUB 5100
1890 GOSUB 6130:BM$="During their lunch, a phone call came for Connors.":GOSUB 5100
1900 BM$="He left the table to answer it, coming back shortly after.":GOSUB 5100
1910 W3=0:GOSUB 6340:BM$="Connors: I'm terribly sorry, but it seems their car broke down, and they\won't be able to make it here right away. They said they might be here this\evening... What do you say?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1920 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: Well, we've waited this long, we might as well keep waiting. Let's take\a room for the night, Susanna.":GOSUB 5100
1930 BM$="Connors went back to the phone booth.":GOSUB 5100
1940 COMMON FO:GOSUB 6180:GOSUB 9010:BM$="David and Susanna reserved a room at the Cathedral Hotel, and then\decided to visit Stonehenge.":GOSUB 5100:'
1950 BM$="Connors would wait in the lobby, in case they contacted him again.":GOSUB 5100
1960 GOSUB 6160:BM$="There were few tourists at Stonehenge, as it was not the weekend. David\was somewhat disappointed that the watchmen would not let anyone inside\the stone circle.":GOSUB 5100
1980 ISET X:BM$="Still, the view made him forget how tiring the tour was. He felt as if he and\Susanna were on their honeymoon.":GOSUB 5100
1990 GOSUB 6170:BM$="The sun was setting, and all the other tourists had left. They returned to\the parking lot, ready to go back to the hotel.":GOSUB 5100
2000 COMMON FO:GOSUB 6200:GOSUB 9035:BM$="David tried starting the car, but the engine would not start. Thinking the\battery might be dead, David opened the hood... and a chill ran down his\spine.":GOSUB 5100
2010 BM$="Someone had torn out the wires.":GOSUB 5100
2020 BM$="David and Susanna stood in front of the car, dumbfounded.":GOSUB 5100
